     <h1>Exercise Name: Incline / Upper Chest Pec Deck Fly (Machine Machine Fly)</h1>
     <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>  
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Incline / Upper Chest Pec Deck Fly (Machine Fly). The video highlights the upper chest muscles (Pectoralis Major — Clavicular Head) in bright glowing colors, illustrating how adjusting the seat height lower or leaning back slightly angles the torso upward to emphasize the upper fibers of the chest for maximum engagement and hypertrophy.
 Exercise Name: Incline / Upper Chest Pec Deck Fly (Machine Machine Fly)
 Target Muscles: Upper Chest (Pectoralis Major — Clavicular Head)
 Secondary Muscles: Anterior Deltoids (front shoulders), Serratus Anterior
</div></div>
<pre><h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1><u><b><h4>Setup:</h4></b></u> Adjust the seat height lower so that the handles align with your upper chest or neck level, or lean slightly back into the seat to angle your torso upward.
 <u><b><h4>Grip & Alignment:</h4></b></u> Grip the vertical handles firmly while keeping a soft, natural bend in your elbows. Keep your upper back and head supported against the pad.
 <u><b><h4>Fly Phase (Concentric):</h4></b></u> Exhale as you pull the handles together in a controlled arc in front of your upper chest. Focus on driving your upper arms toward each other.
 <u><b><h4>Peak Squeeze:</h4></b></u> Pause for a split second at the peak position, squeezing your upper pectoral muscles together.
 <u><b><h4>Return Phase (Eccentric):</h4></b></u> Inhale as you slowly lower the handles back outward under full control, opening your chest until you feel a complete stretch.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Targeted Upper Chest Hypertrophy: </b> Emphasizes the upper fibers of the pectoral muscle to help build a fuller, more complete chest appearance.
 <b>◉Strict Muscle Isolation: </b> Removes tricep assistance and core balance demands, allowing pure focus on chest hypertrophy.
 <b>◉Joint Stability: </b> The guided machine path minimizes strain on shoulder joints compared to incline dumbbell flyes.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Definition | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your elbows elevated and level with the line of pull throughout each rep to maintain continuous tension on your upper chest.
